When a model contains both an equality constraint  between parameters with different names and also contains a defined parameter, parameterEstimates() numbers the parameters non-sequentially (at least in two cases that I have run).  This appears to be related to removing the equality constraints listed in the parameter table between the model parameters and defined parameters.  It appears that this does not affect equality constraints between parameters with the same name because they are listed last.

HS.model <- ' visual  =~ x1 + a*x2 + b*x3
              textual =~ x4 + x5 + x6
              speed   =~ x7 + x8 + x9
              a == b
              nada := 0 '

fit <- cfa(HS.model, data=HolzingerSwineford1939)

parameterEstimates(fit)[24:25,]
dim(parameterEstimates(fit))
lavaanify(HS.model)[21:23,]

Keith
