First off, thanks for this group; it has been infinitely helpful to myself and colleagues while we were teaching a course on SEM.

My questions refer to the int.ov.free argument. In the lavaan() function this is defaulted to FALSE whereas in the sem() and cfa() function it is defaulted to TRUE.

Why does int.ov.free need to be set to TRUE when doing multi-group analyses? I get the same results when set to FALSE as I do when set to TRUE before doing a multi-group analysis, but I get very different results when conducting multi-group analyses such that if it's set to FALSE it's a very poorly fitting model.

